# Prompt for App Creation

Use this prompt to generate or build the app for the `firebase-notepad` repository.

## Goal
Create a working Android app from the existing Expo/React Native project in `app/`, using local Android build tooling without Expo cloud services.

## Instructions
- Keep Expo compatibility and use local native build support.
- Use `npx expo prebuild -p android` if Android native files are not already generated.
- Ensure local Android SDK and JDK 11 are used.
- Generate a signed release APK and place it at `app/app-release.apk`.
- If signing is required, create a keystore and configure `app/android/keystore.properties`.
- Avoid using Expo cloud build services.

## Environment
- Repository root: `/workspaces/firebase-notepad`
- Android project path: `app/android`
- App folder: `app/`

## Commands
```bash
cd /workspaces/firebase-notepad/app
export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64
npm install --legacy-peer-deps
npx expo prebuild -p android
cd android
./gradlew clean assembleRelease --no-daemon
cp app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk ../app-release.apk
```

## Notes
- If `app/android/local.properties` is missing, create it with the Android SDK path.
- If `keystore.properties` is missing, create it and configure `app/android/app/build.gradle` to use it.
- For a one-command build, use the project script defined in `app/package.json` if available.
